link=3D"#0563C1" vlink=3D"#954F72" style=3D'word-wrap:break-word'><div =
class=3DWordSection1><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Current Dev =
Position: YP 4.2 M2</span><o:p></o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Next Deadline: 23rd =
January 2023 YP 4.2 M2 Build</span><o:p></o:p></p><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Next Team =
Meetings:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo7;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Bug Triage meeting Thursday =
January 5th 7:30 am PDT (<a =
href=3D"https://zoom.us/j/454367603?pwd=3DZGxoa2ZXL3FkM3Y0bFd5aVpHVVZ6dz0=
9"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://zoom.us/j/454367603?pwd=3DZGxoa2ZXL3FkM3Y=
0bFd5aVpHVVZ6dz09</span></a>)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo7;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Weekly Project Engineering Sync =
Tuesday January 3rd at 8 am PDT (<a =
href=3D"https://zoom.us/j/990892712?pwd=3DcHU1MjhoM2x6ck81bkcrYjRrcmJsUT0=
9"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://zoom.us/j/990892712?pwd=3DcHU1MjhoM2x6ck8=
1bkcrYjRrcmJsUT09</span></a><a =
href=3D"https://zoom.us/j/990892712"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>)</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo7;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Twitch -&nbsp; See <a =
href=3D"https://www.twitch.tv/theyoctojester"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://www.twitch.tv/theyoctojester</span></a><o=
:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Key =
Status/Updates:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 4.2 M1 and YP 4.0.6 were =
released.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Builds on the autobuilder are =
problematic at present due to connection losses with the controller =
machine. We understand the cause and will be migrating the controller to =
a new server/location in the next maintenance window to address =
this.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A number of invasive bitbake =
changes have merged including a change to add threading to =
bitbake&#8217;s server/cooker. This will allow us to attempt to resolve =
various UI/server hang related open bugs and to improve the user =
experience, e.g. Ctrl+C handling. If people do see issues with hangs, =
please report them and include the tail end of the =
bitbake-cookerdaemon.log file.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The bitbake cache changes to =
optionally include more hash debugging information did merge. This =
currently triggers only for the bitbake -S operations but once that mode =
is triggered for memory resident bitbake, it is &#8220;sticky&#8221; and =
will remain set until it unloads. We have seen some OOM issues on =
autobuilder workers which may be related to this, more debugging is =
needed to check on bitbake&#8217;s memory =
usage.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Automatic bitbake function =
library dependency code has also merged and is active. This should let =
us migrate class code to become library code for performance =
improvements.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A bug in the layer.conf =
variable changes was identified which was causing re-parsing when it =
wasn&#8217;t necessary. A fix has been merged to address =
that.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The OE TSC decided in favour of =
adding export flag expansion despite the performance impact so that =
patch will be queued.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We merged a number of neat rust =
improvements which add on target cargo support and added automated QA =
tests for this functionality so we can ensure it continues to work and =
doesn&#8217;t regress. Thanks Alex Kiernan, we hope to see more series =
like this one!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>CVE levels in master have =
improved but still need a little work<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The autobuilder maintenance =
window is moving from Friday to Monday.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l6 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have a growing number of =
bugs in bugzilla, any help with them is =
appreciated.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'margin-bottom:12.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>As people are likely aware, the =
project has a number of components which are either unmaintained, or =
have people with little to no time trying to keep them alive. These =
components include: patchtest, layerindex, devtool, toaster, wic, oeqa, =
autobuilder, CROPs containers, pseudo and more. Many have open bugs. =
Help is welcome in trying to better look after these =
components!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs identified as =
possible for newcomers to the project: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers</spa=
n></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs that are =
currently unassigned for YP 4.2. See: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Medium.2B_4.1_Unass=
igned_Enhancements.2FBugs"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Med=
ium.2B_4.2_Unassigned_Enhancements.2FBugs</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></l=
i><li style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We&#8217;d welcome new =
maintainers for recipes in OE-Core. Please see the list at: <a =
href=3D"http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/meta/conf/distro/i=
nclude/maintainers.inc"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/me=
ta/conf/distro/include/maintainers.inc</span></a> and discuss with the =
existing maintainer, or ask on the OE-Core mailing list. We will likely =
move a chunk of these to &#8220;Unassigned&#8221; soon to help =
facilitate this.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Help is very much welcome in =
trying to resolve our autobuilder intermittent issues. You can see the =
list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a>.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l9 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Help us resolve CVE issues: <a =
href=3D"https://autobuilder.yocto.io/pub/non-release/patchmetrics/"><span=
 style=3D'color:#1155CC'>CVE =
metrics</span></a>&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
